@using System.Globalization
@*
    Shared Home/Index placeholder.

    Exists so all three hosts serve an identical landing page before real controllers are
    ported, which is what keeps the skeleton at parity. Api.Gate previously had its own
    copy and Api.Application had none at all, so "/" 404'd in one portal and not the
    other. Replace with the real HomeController once the corrected legacy sources land.

    Arabic text is deliberately not written inline here: non-ASCII does not survive
    reliably through editing tooling, so the strings live in ISCC.Shared.Web.ViewText.
    Real application copy belongs in the .resx files under ISCC.Shared.Localization and
    should be resolved through IStringLocalizer.
*@
@{
    var culture = CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture;
}
<h1>@ISCC.Shared.Web.ViewText.PortalName(culture)</h1>
<p>@ISCC.Shared.Web.ViewText.NoPagesMigratedYet(culture)</p>
